; Turn a braille-ready file into something to read.
;
; From a tester working on .brf files. Two things worth copying:
;
; The print page indicator becomes a space and an x and the page number, so
; a print page can still be found. The Replace value is QUOTED, which is how
; a leading or trailing space survives -- a value on one line is trimmed
; otherwise, and the space would be lost.
;
; Order matters: the page indicators are handled before the blank lines they
; leave behind are tidied away.

[print page numbers]
Find="\n-{5,}\s*(\d+)"
Replace=" x$1"

[form feeds]
Find="\f"
Replace=""

[runs of blank lines]
Find="\n{3,}"
Replace="\n\n"
